<main class="hs-page">
  <nav class="hs-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><div class="hs-wrap"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/articles/">Articles</a><span>/</span>Harj Singh</div></nav>
  <section class="hs-hero" aria-labelledby="hs-name">
    <div class="hs-wrap hs-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="hs-label hs-eyebrow">CallTeam · Author &amp; editor</div>
        <h1 id="hs-name">Harj <span>Singh.</span></h1>
        <p class="hs-role">B2B Writer, Editor &amp; Sales Practitioner</p>
        <p class="hs-intro">Twenty years in sales. A practical perspective on how businesses buy, how sellers earn a conversation and what makes the next step worthwhile.</p>
        <div class="hs-actions"><a class="hs-action hs-action-primary" href="#hs-method">Explore the methodology <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="hs-action" href="#hs-background">Read the background</a></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="hs-identity" aria-label="Experience at a glance">
        <div class="hs-identity-top"><span class="hs-label">The work behind the words</span><span>CALLTEAM</span></div>
        <div class="hs-monogram" aria-hidden="true">H<i>S</i></div>
        <div class="hs-identity-bottom"><div><strong>20 years</strong><span>Sales experience</span></div><div><strong>Fortune 100<br>&amp; Fortune 500</strong><span>Experience in enterprise environments</span></div></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="hs-experience-strip"><div class="hs-wrap hs-strip-inner"><div><strong>Banking &amp; financial services</strong><span>Trust, risk and commercial decisions</span></div><div><strong>SaaS &amp; B2B sales</strong><span>Workflows, stakeholders and adoption</span></div><div><strong>Outbound calling</strong><span>Research, conversations and qualification</span></div><div><strong>Sales training</strong><span>Coaching, feedback and execution</span></div></div></div>

  <section class="hs-section" id="hs-background" aria-labelledby="hs-background-title"><div class="hs-wrap">
    <div class="hs-section-heading"><span class="hs-label">01 / Background</span><h2 id="hs-background-title">A sales career behind<br>every practical question.</h2></div>
    <div class="hs-background"><p class="hs-background-note">Harj Singh writes and edits B2B sales guidance for CallTeam.</p><div class="hs-body-copy"><p>His background spans 20 years in banking, financial services, SaaS, outbound sales and sales training, including experience in Fortune 100 and Fortune 500 environments. That experience shapes his approach to prospecting, qualification, buyer conversations and the management of sales work.</p><p>At CallTeam, his writing helps business owners, revenue leaders and sales teams make informed decisions about cold calling, appointment setting and outsourced sales development. He brings the same practical questions to a buying guide, a call script and a training discussion: who is involved, what needs to change and what would make a conversation useful?</p></div></div>
    <div class="hs-experience-grid"><article><h3>Banking &amp; financial services</h3><p>A perspective shaped by commercial responsibility, careful claims and the trust required to discuss consequential business decisions.</p></article><article><h3>SaaS &amp; complex B2B sales</h3><p>Attention to the buyer's working environment, the people involved in a decision and the effort required to adopt a new service or system.</p></article><article><h3>Calling &amp; sales training</h3><p>A focus on preparation, listening, useful questions and coaching that a seller can apply in the next conversation.</p></article></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="hs-method" id="hs-method" aria-labelledby="hs-method-title"><div class="hs-wrap">
    <div class="hs-section-heading"><span class="hs-label">02 / Working methodology</span><h2 id="hs-method-title">From a buyer's question<br>to a useful next step.</h2></div>
    <p class="hs-method-intro">Harj's approach connects research, sales experience and editorial judgment. The work begins with a specific situation and follows it through to a decision the reader can make.</p>
    <ol class="hs-method-grid" aria-label="Four stages of Harj Singh's editorial approach">
      <li><span class="hs-step-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Understand the buyer</h3><p>Identify the role, the current approach and the reason someone would consider a change. Define the question the guide needs to answer.</p><div class="hs-step-output">Output: a clear buying situation</div></li>
      <li><span class="hs-step-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Check the evidence</h3><p>Examine relevant sources, service details and campaign examples. Separate reported results, practical judgment and illustrative scenarios.</p><div class="hs-step-output">Output: claims with context</div></li>
      <li><span class="hs-step-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Make it usable</h3><p>Translate the findings into natural language, specific questions and examples. Consider how the advice would work in a real sales conversation.</p><div class="hs-step-output">Output: guidance a person can apply</div></li>
      <li><span class="hs-step-num" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Define the next step</h3><p>Explain what to check, who to involve and what a useful meeting or evaluation should resolve. Give the reader a practical way forward.</p><div class="hs-step-output">Output: an informed action</div></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="hs-feedback"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 8a8 8 0 1 0 1 7M19 3v5h-5"/></svg><span>Buyer questions and new evidence feed the next review of the guidance.</span></div>
    <p class="hs-method-caption">A working approach to B2B writing, campaign guidance and sales training.</p>
  </div></section>

  <div class="hs-principle"><div class="hs-wrap hs-principle-inner"><span class="hs-label">The editorial standard</span><p>A useful sales article should leave you knowing what to ask, what to check and what to do next.</p></div></div>

  <section class="hs-section" aria-labelledby="hs-topics-title"><div class="hs-wrap">
    <div class="hs-section-heading"><span class="hs-label">03 / Areas of focus</span><h2 id="hs-topics-title">The decisions behind<br>better sales work.</h2></div>
    <div class="hs-topics">
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">01</span><h3>B2B cold calling</h3><p>Account preparation, opening questions, objection handling and conversations that respect the buyer's situation.</p></article>
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">02</span><h3>Appointment setting</h3><p>Buyer fit, meeting purpose, qualification, follow-up and the context a salesperson needs before taking the call.</p></article>
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">03</span><h3>Sales training</h3><p>Call review, discovery, coaching and practical changes that help sellers improve their day-to-day execution.</p></article>
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">04</span><h3>Outsourced sales development</h3><p>Campaign scope, provider selection, internal responsibilities and the work required to keep outreach running.</p></article>
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">05</span><h3>Financial services sales</h3><p>Trust, stakeholder involvement, evidence and precise language when the product or service carries meaningful risk.</p></article>
      <article class="hs-topic"><span class="hs-topic-index">06</span><h3>SaaS buying conversations</h3><p>Current workflows, existing vendors, implementation concerns and the business reason for a product evaluation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="hs-section hs-ai-section" aria-labelledby="hs-ai-title"><div class="hs-wrap">
    <div class="hs-section-heading"><span class="hs-label">04 / Research</span><h2 id="hs-ai-title">AI-assisted research.</h2></div>
    <div class="hs-background"><div aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="hs-body-copy"><p>AI helps organise research and identify questions for further investigation. Harj checks important claims against source material and takes responsibility for the articles published under his name.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="hs-section" aria-labelledby="hs-standards-title"><div class="hs-wrap">
    <div class="hs-section-heading"><span class="hs-label">05 / Writing &amp; editing</span><h2 id="hs-standards-title">Specific advice.<br>Clear boundaries.</h2></div>
    <ul class="hs-standard-list"><li><span>01</span><h3>Explain who the advice fits</h3><p>Identify the buyer, market and conditions that make the guidance relevant. Account for situations where a different approach may work better.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Keep evidence attached</h3><p>Connect factual claims to sources where available. Give campaign results their scope and timeframe, and label hypothetical examples clearly.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Write in simple English</h3><p>Use direct explanations, natural questions and practical examples. Remove repetition and give technical terms enough context to be useful.</p></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Make the commercial role clear</h3><p>CallTeam publishes sales guidance and provides sales services. Recommendations should explain the relevant fit, responsibilities and next step.</p></li></ul>
  </div></section>

